  "passage": "The annual Summer Science Fair at Riverside School was a big success this year. Over 100 students participated, and registration was smooth, with only a few slightly delayed forms. One highlight was the potato-growing competition, where students displayed their harvests and explained how they cared for their plants. Unfortunately, Sarah's entry was missing a key diagram that showed her experiment's results, so she couldn't complete her presentation fully. During the event, Tom, who had been feeling unwell earlier in the day, had to leave early to rest. Despite these minor issues, everyone enjoyed the hands-on activities, like building simple machines, and learned a lot about science and teamwork. The fair ended with prizes for the best projects, and teachers praised the students for their hard work. Plans are already underway for next year's event, which promises to be even bigger.",
